  "nl_text": "The database schema named rschema_0434 consists of five tables: User, Maze, Skybox, Map, and User_Game_Record.\nThe User table is used to store user information. It contains five columns: Email (a string of up to 255 characters), Password (also a string of up to 255 characters), Registration_Time (a date and time), User_ID (an integer), and Username (a string of up to 255 characters). The User_ID is the primary key of this table.\nThe Maze table is used to store maze information. It contains five columns: Creation_Date (a date and time), Description (a string of up to 255 characters), Last_Modified_Date (a date and time), Maze_ID (an integer), and Name (a string of up to 255 characters). The Maze_ID is the primary key of this table.\nThe Skybox table is used to store skybox information. It contains six columns: Creation_Date (a date and time), Description (a string of up to 255 characters), File_Path (a string of up to 255 characters), Last_Modified_Date (a date and time), Name (a string of up to 255 characters), and Skybox_ID (an integer). The Skybox_ID is the primary key of this table.\nThe Map table is used to store map information. It contains six columns: Associated_Maze_ID (an integer), Creation_Date (a date and time), Last_Modified_Date (a date and time), Map_Data (a binary large object), Map_ID (an integer), and Name (a string of up to 255 characters). The Map_ID is the primary key of this table, and the Associated_Maze_ID is a foreign key referencing the Maze table.\nFinally, the User_Game_Record table is used to store user game records. It contains nine columns: Game_Creation_Time (a date and time), Game_End_Time (a date and time), Game_Last_Modified_Time (a date and time), Game_Start_Time (a date and time), Game_Status (a string of up to 255 characters), Maze_ID (an integer), User_ID (an integer), User_Score (an integer), and the combination of User_ID and Maze_ID is the primary key. The Maze_ID and User_ID are foreign keys referencing the Maze and User tables, respectively.\nThis schema ensures data integrity by enforcing primary and foreign key constraints, and by allowing null values in some columns. It also includes indexes on the foreign keys to optimize database performance.",
  "gold_question": "The functional requirements for a virtual maze game platform are as follows: The system shall manage user basic information, including User ID, Username, Password, Email, and Registration Date. The platform shall provide maze creation functionality, with maze information including Maze ID, Name, Description, Creation Date, and Last Modified Date. Each maze may contain multiple maps, with map information including Map ID, Associated Maze ID, Name, Map Data (e.g., in JSON format), Creation Date, and Last Modified Date. The system shall also support skybox management, with skybox information including Skybox ID, Name, File Path, Description, Creation Date, and Last Modified Date. Users can participate in maze games, with game information including User ID, Maze ID, User Score, Game Start Time, Game End Time, Game Status (e.g., In Progress, Completed, Failed), and Game Creation and Last Modified Date.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0434.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0434\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `registration_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `maze` (\n  `maze_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `creation_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `last_modified_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`maze_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `skybox` (\n  `skybox_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `file_path` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `last_modified_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`skybox_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `map` (\n  `map_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `map_data` blob DEFAULT NULL,\n  `creation_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `last_modified_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `associated_maze_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`map_id`),\n  KEY `fk_associated_maze` (`associated_maze_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `map_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`associated_maze_id`) REFERENCES `maze` (`maze_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_game_record` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `maze_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `game_creation_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `game_start_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `game_end_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `game_last_modified_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `game_status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `user_score` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `maze_id`),\n  KEY `fk_user` (`user_id`),\n  KEY `fk_maze` (`maze_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_game_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_game_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`maze_id`) REFERENCES `maze` (`maze_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
